---
/**
 * TestimonialsBand — the `.testi` band: a centred head (eyebrow, <h2>, a row
 * of five stars, a paragraph), the sage "Read More on Google" button, and the
 * draggable <ReviewMarquee> of the whole reviews collection, newest first.
 *
 * ONE COMPONENT, THREE KEYS. The shape ships on three routes and the three
 * templates are clones of one another, element for element:
 *
 *   src/pages/index.astro:601-614                 home_testimonials (no id)
 *   src/pages/about-us/index.astro:732-749        about_us_voices  (#voices)
 *   src/pages/patient-testimonials/index.astro:386-399
 *                                                  patient_testimonials_reviews (#reviews)
 *
 * registered in src/blocks/CodeSectionBlock.astro. Every difference between
 * the three was read off those lines and is reproduced by a prop, never by a
 * guess — the table is the contract:
 *
 *   difference                          home        patient-testimonials  about-us
 *   ─────────────────────────────────── ─────────── ───────────────────── ─────────────────
 *   `id` on <section>                   none        "reviews"             "voices"
 *   eyebrow element                     span.eyebrow span.eyebrow         <Eyebrow center>
 *   h2 carries data-vs-reveal-lines     no          no                    yes
 *   .stars carries aria-hidden="true"   no          no                    yes
 *   eyebrow fallback                    "Testimonials" none               "Testimonials"
 *   heading fallback                    "5-Star <em>Smiles</em>" none     none
 *   body fallback                       (sentence)  none                  none
 *
 * The three about-us rows travel together under ONE flag, `eyebrowComponent`,
 * because they are one variant (the page's author drew that band with the
 * shared Eyebrow component and the reveal-lines/aria-hidden pair in the same
 * edit, about-us/index.astro:735-737) and no page ships any other mix.
 *
 * ── D1: a route-scoped band reads its own page ────────────────────────────
 * The words are live Section-copy rows (sectionId "testimonials" | "reviews" |
 * "voices"), edited in wp-admin under Pages -> the page -> Section copy, and a
 * code band receives props only. Freezing them in the BANDS entry would make
 * three live rows dead. So this component calls
 * `getPageContent(Astro.url.pathname)` itself — the read every one of the
 * three templates runs (index.astro:54, about-us/index.astro:49,
 * patient-testimonials/index.astro:47) — guarded by the `route` prop: on any
 * other route it renders NOTHING and warns, because the row it asks for lives
 * on that page's entry. Decision D1, 2026-09-08.
 *
 * ── Fallback semantics, byte for byte ─────────────────────────────────────
 * The home template writes `section("testimonials").eyebrow || "Testimonials"`
 * (index.astro:604-607) and the other two write `section("reviews").eyebrow`
 * with no `||` at all (patient-testimonials/index.astro:389-392;
 * about-us/index.astro:736-738 for heading and body). `pick()` below is that
 * distinction: a fallback that was PASSED is applied with `||` exactly as the
 * template did; a fallback that was NOT passed leaves the live value alone,
 * including an empty string — so patient-testimonials keeps rendering
 * `<span class="eyebrow"></span>` when its row's eyebrow is blank, as it does
 * today, rather than growing a word the template never had.
 *
 * ── What is a prop and why ────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * The Google button (label, href, hover) and the marquee's aria-label are
 * literals in all three templates (index.astro:610/613,
 * about-us/index.astro:741-745/748, patient-testimonials/index.astro:395/398).
 * The href is a pasted external URL, which the HREF policy keeps out of
 * WordPress fields (src/blocks/cta.ts:14-18); D7 backlogs a Practice-Settings
 * URL for it. Until then it lives in the BANDS entry, as the templates had it.
 *
 * ── Markup ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Verbatim from the three ranges above: `section.testi[id?]` > `.wrap` >
 * `.testi-head[data-vs-reveal-batch]` (eyebrow, <h2> via set:html, `.stars`
 * ★★★★★, <p>) + `.testi-actions[data-vs-reveal]` (sage Button); then
 * <ReviewMarquee> OUTSIDE `.wrap`, as the templates place it. The band is
 * wrapped in `{onRoute && (…)}` so that off-route it emits nothing, and that
 * wrapper is why the `{" "}` spacers exist: measured with @astrojs/compiler
 * (compact, 2026-09-08), the template's static nesting compiles to ONE SPACE
 * between every pair of tags, while an element tree inside an expression
 * compiles with NO whitespace at all. Each `{" "}` puts back the exact space
 * the static template emits, so the bytes match; remove one and the build
 * differs by a byte.
 *
 * `data-vs-reveal-lines` and `aria-hidden` are dynamic, so they go through
 * addAttribute: `""` renders the bare attribute (` data-vs-reveal-lines`) and
 * `undefined` renders nothing — `true` would render `="true"`, which is not
 * what about-us ships (node_modules/astro/dist/runtime/server/render/util.js:75-87).
 *
 * ── CSS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * home.css:870-888 and the 780px rule at :977, restated below; about-us.css
 * :416-430/:488 and patient-testimonials.css:479-495/:547 are the same rules
 * with the same values (about-us omits the `.eyebrow` pair because its
 * eyebrow is the global `.vs-eyebrow.vs-center`, global.css:554-566 — that
 * element carries neither `.eyebrow` nor this component's scope, so the pair
 * below does not reach it, exactly as before). Astro scopes by attribute on
 * EVERY compound, so a rule rooted at `.home` would become
 * `.home[data-astro-cid-…] .testi[data-astro-cid-…]` and never match — the
 * page root is not this component's element. Everything is therefore rooted
 * at `.testi`, and the section's own rule is written `section.testi` so it
 * lands at (0,2,1) against the page sheets' `.home .testi` /
 * `.aus .testi` / `.patient-testimonials .testi` at (0,2,0): a win on every
 * page, with the same values, and its own 780px breakpoint because a page's
 * breakpoint can no longer reach it (memory: page CSS cannot beat block CSS;
 * CodeSectionBlock.astro:437-439). The page sheets' aliases `--paper` and
 * `--sage` map 1:1 to `--vs-paper` / `--vs-sage` on all three roots
 * (home.css:18,24; about-us.css:12,16; patient-testimonials.css:14,18), so
 * the `--vs-*` names are used here. `.wrap`, `.eyebrow`'s type styles and the
 * h2 colour stay with the page sheets — they are not in the cited ranges and
 * the band still sits inside the page root.
 */
import { getCollection, type CollectionEntry } from "astro:content";
import Button from "./Button.astro";
import Eyebrow from "./Eyebrow.astro";
import ReviewMarquee from "./ReviewMarquee.astro";
import { getPageContent } from "../lib/page-content";

interface Props {
  /**
   * The route this band belongs to ("/", "/about-us/", "/patient-testimonials/").
   * It reads that page's Section-copy row, so on any other route it renders
   * nothing and warns.
   */
  route: string;
  /** The DOM id, fed by PageBlocks through the row's anchor. Absent when blank. */
  id?: string;
  /** The Section-copy row this band reads: "testimonials" | "reviews" | "voices". */
  sectionId: string;
  /** Applied with `||` when passed; when absent the live value stands, blank included. */
  eyebrowFallback?: string;
  /** Same rule. May carry inline markup (`<em>`) — it renders through set:html. */
  headingFallback?: string;
  /** Same rule. */
  bodyFallback?: string;
  /** The sage button under the head — label, href and hover label. */
  ctaLabel: string;
  ctaHref: string;
  ctaHover: string;
  /** The marquee's aria-label. */
  marqueeLabel: string;
  /**
   * about-us's variant: `<Eyebrow center>` instead of `span.eyebrow`, the
   * <h2> marked `data-vs-reveal-lines`, the stars `aria-hidden="true"`
   * (about-us/index.astro:735-737). Off by default — home and
   * patient-testimonials draw the bare span.
   */
  eyebrowComponent?: boolean;
}

const {
  route,
  id,
  sectionId,
  eyebrowFallback,
  headingFallback,
  bodyFallback,
  ctaLabel,
  ctaHref,
  ctaHover,
  marqueeLabel,
  eyebrowComponent = false,
} = Astro.props;

// trailingSlash is 'always' (astro.config.mjs:375); normalise both sides anyway
// so "/about-us" and "/about-us/" name the same page, as page-content.ts does.
const withSlash = (p: string) => (p.endsWith("/") ? p : `${p}/`);
const here = Astro.url.pathname;
const onRoute = withSlash(here) === withSlash(route);

if (!onRoute) {
  console.warn(
    `[blocks] TestimonialsBand is scoped to ${route} and was asked to render on ${here} — it reads that page's Section copy, so it renders nothing here`,
  );
}

/** The template's `live || fallback` when a fallback was passed; `live` alone when not. */
const pick = (live: string, fallback?: string) =>
  fallback === undefined ? live : live || fallback;

let eyebrow = "";
let heading = "";
let body = "";
let reviews: CollectionEntry<"reviews">[] = [];
if (onRoute) {
  const { section } = await getPageContent(here);
  const row = section(sectionId);
  eyebrow = pick(row.eyebrow, eyebrowFallback);
  heading = pick(row.heading, headingFallback);
  body = pick(row.body, bodyFallback);
  // Newest first — the sort all three templates run (index.astro:32-33,
  // about-us/index.astro:360, patient-testimonials/index.astro:29-30; the
  // ReviewsBand.astro:55-57 idiom).
  reviews = (await getCollection("reviews")).sort(
    (a, b) => +b.data.date - +a.data.date,
  );
}
---

{
  onRoute && (
    <section class="testi" id={id}>{" "}
      <div class="wrap">{" "}
        <div class="testi-head" data-vs-reveal-batch>{" "}
          {eyebrowComponent ? <Eyebrow center>{eyebrow}</Eyebrow> : <span class="eyebrow">{eyebrow}</span>}{" "}
          <h2 data-vs-reveal-lines={eyebrowComponent ? "" : undefined}><Fragment set:html={heading} /></h2>{" "}
          <div class="stars" aria-hidden={eyebrowComponent ? "true" : undefined}>★★★★★</div>{" "}
          <p>{body}</p>{" "}
        </div>{" "}
        <div class="testi-actions" data-vs-reveal>{" "}
          <Button variant="sage" href={ctaHref} hoverLabel={ctaHover}>{ctaLabel}</Button>{" "}
        </div>{" "}
      </div>{" "}
      <ReviewMarquee reviews={reviews} ariaLabel={marqueeLabel} />{" "}
    </section>
  )
}

<style>
  /* home.css:870 (= about-us.css:416, patient-testimonials.css:479).
     `section.testi` so the scoped rule is (0,2,1) against the page sheets'
     `.<page> .testi` (0,2,0) — a win, not a tie. Same values. */
  section.testi { padding: 140px 0; background: var(--vs-paper); overflow: hidden; }
  /* home.css:871 (= about-us.css:417, patient-testimonials.css:480) */
  .testi .testi-head { text-align: center; max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto 60px; }
  /* home.css:872-875 (= patient-testimonials.css:481-485; about-us has no
     `.eyebrow` here — its eyebrow is the global `.vs-eyebrow.vs-center`). */
  .testi .testi-head .eyebrow { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; }
  .testi .testi-head .eyebrow::before, .testi .testi-head .eyebrow::after {
    content: ""; width: 28px; height: 1px; background: var(--vs-sage);
  }
  /* home.css:876-878 (= about-us.css:421-423, patient-testimonials.css:486-488) */
  .testi .testi-head h2 { margin: 22px 0 22px; }
  .testi .testi-head p { font-size: 17px; }
  .testi .testi-head .stars { margin-top: 18px; color: var(--vs-sage); font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: .3em; }
  /* home.css:884-888 (= about-us.css:426-430, patient-testimonials.css:491-495) */
  .testi .testi-actions {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    margin-top: 40px;
  }

  /* home.css:977 inside the 780 block at :934 (= about-us.css:488 in :465,
     patient-testimonials.css:547 in :519). */
  @media (max-width: 780px) {
    section.testi { padding: 80px 0; }
  }
</style>
